SlothClash core patch 0040: listener close data races.

The accept and read loops of 20 inbound listeners (socks tcp/udp, http, mixed,
redir, tproxy tcp/udp, tunnel tcp/udp, shadowsocks tcp/udp, sing_shadowsocks,
sing_vmess, sing_vless, trojan, snell, anytls, sudoku, tuic, shadowquic) read a
plain `closed bool` after Accept/ReadFrom fails, while Close writes it from
another goroutine. `go test -race` reports it whenever a listener is closed
twice (the chain-group tests of patch 0006 do that). The flag becomes an
atomic.Bool; nothing else changes. Listeners that only write the flag
(sing_hysteria2, hysteria2_realm, sing_tun, trusttunnel) are left alone.

Own code (SlothClash), GPL-3.0 like mihomo. Test:
listener/close_race_test.go (fails under -race without the change).

